Subject: Cantor M2B Supplied Directory Topology Projection Source

Description: Raw selected build source for one pure projection that turns a caller-supplied directory stability input and caller-declared descendant placement into a complete M2A directory form while preserving exact lineage and making no physical, traversal, inventory, receipt, or admission claim.

& [SourceIdentity] is selected and unprocessed
  + [source_uuid] is fde99cce-e274-458c-aee1-a1d565c432eb
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is 3546eb38-36a5-4d88-8097-ecb86b5b40a0
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [captured_at] is 2026-07-31
  + [working_profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-directory-topology-projection/0.1
  + [selection_review_uuid] is 7d0ae4a1-508a-4235-ae47-002599d51145
  + [authority_state] is preserved_source_only_after_manifest_binding

& [Purpose] is close one supplied structural directory carrier
  + accept one strict caller placement plan
  + accept one complete WindowsSuppliedEntryStabilityInput by value
  + invoke the current supplied-entry stability reconciler inside the projection path
  + reject any non-directory result
  + join the plan to the revalidated pair through exact entry-reference and final-component equality
  + construct one complete current-M2A directory TopologyEntryObservation
  + preserve the complete plan, revalidated stable pair, and completed topology observation in one output-only wrapper
  - never: accept a bare WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair as sufficient input
  - never: perform or imply physical observation

& [WhyThisSlice] is dependency ordered
  + the regular-file supplied structural carrier is complete and proven
  + the supplied assembly seed already represents directories without length or digest
  + the supplied stability reconciler already compares directory facts under its declared supplied-value semantics
  + M2A already defines the complete structural directory shape
  + a complete directory carrier is required before a later mixed-entry inventory may be coherently represented
  + physical production remains a larger unsafe-adjacent contract and is not needed to prove this pure composition

& [CriticalProvenanceRule] forbids direct stable-pair trust
  + WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair is currently a public Serialize and Deserialize data form
  + callers can construct that form without executing the current stability reconciler
  + accepting it directly would let a forged or stale lower success enter a new non-forgeable wrapper
  + the new operation therefore accepts WindowsSuppliedEntryStabilityInput and calls reconcile_windows_supplied_entry_stability itself
  + the exact nested stability fault must survive if lower reconciliation rejects
  + the successful stable pair returned by the current reconciler becomes the sole metadata source for projection

& [PlacementPlan] is strict caller syntax
  + [profile] exact cantor-windows-supplied-directory-topology-projection/0.1
  + [projection_identity] nonzero unsigned 64-bit caller-local identity
  + [entry_reference_identity] nonzero unsigned 64-bit correlation identity
  + [relative_path] caller-declared descendant path to be checked by current M2A validation
  + [observation_ordinal] nonzero unsigned 64-bit caller-declared ordinal
  + [encoded_plan_maximum_bytes] is 262144 before JSON decoding
  + unknown JSON fields reject
  + missing, malformed, or type-invalid fields reject
  + no mode field exists because directory mode is fixed by this profile
  + no digest or length field exists because directory shape forbids both

& [Inputs] are complete and bounded by existing contracts
  + [plan] is WindowsSuppliedDirectoryTopologyProjectionPlan
  + [stability_input] is WindowsSuppliedEntryStabilityInput
  + stability input retains both complete supplied assembly inputs
  + existing assembly and stability limits remain authoritative for nested values
  + no bare observation, stable pair, seed, topology observation, or asserted digest is accepted as the evidence carrier

& [EvaluationOrder] is deterministic and fail closed
  + [step_1] validate the placement plan profile, encoded bound when decoded, identities, and ordinal
  + [step_2] invoke current reconcile_windows_supplied_entry_stability on the complete supplied stability input
  + [step_3] require exact plan entry-reference equality with the successful stable pair
  + [step_4] derive the topology projection seed from the successful stable pair pre-read
  + [step_5] require seed kind Directory
  + [step_6] map exact seed-supported fields plus caller placement into one candidate M2A topology observation
  + [step_7] invoke current ValidateTopologyForm on the candidate
  + [step_8] obtain the final component only from the M2A-validated descendant relative path
  + [step_9] require exact byte-for-byte final-component equality with the stable pre-read policy component
  + [step_10] release one complete output-only wrapper
  + first failure terminates evaluation
  + no failure returns partial successful state

& [ExactMapping] distinguishes evidence grades
  + [kind] is Directory from the stable pre-read projection seed
  + [mode_class] is TopologyModeClass Directory fixed by the profile
  + [attributes] copies exact seed attributes
  + [identity] copies exact seed strong identity
  + [number_of_links] copies exact seed link count
  + [streams] copies exact seed stream vector without invention
  + [length] is None
  + [content_sha256] is None
  + [relative_path] copies the plan declaration
  + [observation_ordinal] copies the plan declaration
  + [projection_identity] remains wrapper plan metadata and is not inserted into M2A
  + [entry_reference_identity] remains wrapper plan and stable-pair correlation metadata and is not inserted into M2A

& [DirectoryShape] is exact
  + the revalidated seed must be TopologyEntryKind Directory
  + mode is always TopologyModeClass Directory
  + relative path must be a current-M2A-valid descendant path
  + length is absent
  + content digest is absent
  + stable supplied assembly already requires directory-compatible case-sensitivity and stream facts
  + root directory is not represented by this contract
  - never: translate a directory seed into RootDirectory
  - never: synthesize content length zero or an empty-content hash

& [ReferenceJoin] is exact equality only
  + plan entry-reference identity must be nonzero
  + successful stable-pair entry-reference identity is established by current stability reconciliation
  + the two values must be exactly equal
  + mismatch rejects before topology form construction
  + equality is a caller-supplied structural correlation only
  - never: call equality proof of physical object identity, handle continuity, path identity, or time

& [ComponentJoin] is exact equality only
  + current M2A validation must first accept the descendant relative path
  + final component is the substring after the final forward slash, or the whole one-component descendant path
  + final component must equal stable pre-read policy-decision component exactly
  + comparison is case sensitive and byte exact over Rust strings
  + mismatch rejects
  + successful equality does not prove the physical path was resolved or traversed

& [CurrentM2AValidation] is mandatory
  + construct one candidate TopologyEntryObservation only from the closed mapping
  + invoke its current ValidateTopologyForm implementation
  + preserve the exact TopologyFormFault as a compact nested fault
  + do not duplicate or weaken the M2A path, identity, link, stream, kind, mode, length, digest, or ordinal rules
  + later M2A rule changes must be observed by this projection through the current validator

& [SuccessWrapper] is output only
  + [name] is WindowsSuppliedDirectoryTopologyProjection
  + fields are private
  + wrapper derives Serialize but not Deserialize
  + wrapper has no Default implementation
  + wrapper has no public constructor
  + wrapper has immutable getters for profile, plan, stable pair, and topology observation
  + wrapper preserves the complete placement plan
  + wrapper preserves the complete revalidated WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair
  + wrapper preserves the complete validated TopologyEntryObservation
  + wrapper has no From or Into conversion that drops lineage or evidence grade

& [FaultVocabulary] is closed
  + [json] malformed, unknown, missing, or type-invalid plan JSON
  + [profile] unsupported plan profile
  + [projection_identity] zero projection identity
  + [entry_reference_identity] zero plan entry reference
  + [stability] nested current stability reconciliation failure
  + [entry_reference] plan and successful stable-pair reference mismatch
  + [kind] successful pair is not a directory
  + [topology_form] nested current M2A validation failure
  + [component] final relative-path component mismatch
  + [ordinal] zero observation ordinal
  + [resource] encoded plan exceeds the cap or an impossible post-validation extraction invariant fails
  + fault code is a closed enum
  + nested stability and topology faults remain distinct
  + field text is capped at 64 Unicode scalar values
  + message text is capped at 256 Unicode scalar values
  + faults serialize deterministically
  + no fault contains a successful projection

& [Functions] are minimal
  + decode_windows_supplied_directory_topology_projection_plan accepts bounded bytes and returns a validated plan or fault
  + decode_and_project_windows_supplied_directory_topology accepts plan bytes plus stability input and returns projection or fault
  + project_windows_supplied_directory_topology accepts a plan plus stability input and returns projection or fault
  + private plan validation and bounded-text helpers support those paths only

& [PurityBoundary] is strict
  + deterministic in-memory transformation only
  + no unsafe code
  + no Windows API
  + no filesystem or path-resolution API
  + no process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, model, or tool call
  + no Cargo dependency or lockfile change
  + no physical fixture
  + no candidate admission, mutation, seal, test execution, cleanup, or promotion

& [EvidenceGrades] remain explicit
  + [supplied] both lower metadata assemblies originate as caller-provided values
  + [revalidated] the current pure assembly and stability rules have executed in this call
  + [derived] topology seed fields are deterministic transforms of the revalidated supplied pair
  + [declared] path, ordinal, projection identity, and plan reference are caller syntax
  + [correlated] reference and component values passed exact structural equality gates
  + [projected] the candidate passed current M2A structural validation
  + [physical] absent
  + [complete_inventory] absent
  + [admitted] absent

& [SemanticNonclaims] are mandatory
  - never: claim supplied records came from Windows, a filesystem, a directory handle, or one physical object
  - never: claim pre-read occurred before post-read or both came from the same handle or epoch
  - never: claim the relative path exists, is rooted, was resolved, or names the supplied identity
  - never: claim the ordinal came from enumeration or traversal
  - never: claim directory streams were physically queried or complete
  - never: claim root membership, canonical ordering, duplicate freedom, inventory completeness, or aggregate digest
  - never: claim Git state, executable mode, receipt issuance, candidate admission, mutation safety, or promotion authority

& [RequirementSet] is proposed
  + [M2B-SDTP-001] strict bounded placement-plan decoding and validation
  + [M2B-SDTP-002] complete supplied stability input is the only lower evidence input
  + [M2B-SDTP-003] current stability reconciliation is mandatory and exact faults are nested
  + [M2B-SDTP-004] exact nonzero entry-reference correlation
  + [M2B-SDTP-005] directory-only kind and fixed-mode discipline
  + [M2B-SDTP-006] exact closed field mapping with no digest or length invention
  + [M2B-SDTP-007] current M2A validation is mandatory and exact faults are nested
  + [M2B-SDTP-008] exact final-component correlation after M2A validation
  + [M2B-SDTP-009] output-only complete lineage wrapper
  + [M2B-SDTP-010] closed bounded deterministic fault surface and atomic failure
  + [M2B-SDTP-011] explicit evidence grades and semantic nonclaims
  + [M2B-SDTP-012] zero-effect and zero-dependency implementation boundary
  + [M2B-SDTP-013] focused, static, global, quality, audit, and recursive evidence closure

& [TestObligations] are direct
  + strict JSON rejects unknown fields, malformed data, oversized encoding, wrong profile, and zero identities or ordinal
  + nested stability failure is exact and distinguishable
  + direct stable-pair input is absent from every public projection function
  + regular-file stability input rejects at the directory kind gate
  + plan reference mismatch rejects
  + invalid path reaches and preserves the current nested M2A fault
  + final-component mismatch rejects after M2A validation
  + valid one-component and multi-component descendant paths project exactly
  + output preserves the complete plan and successful stable pair
  + output JSON preserves complete nested lineage and topology form
  + static test proves private output fields, absence of Deserialize and public constructor, mandatory reconciler call, current validator call, fixed directory mapping, and forbidden effect vocabulary
  + focused tests pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + workspace regression and quality gates pass
  + clone-portable evidence hashes every cited artifact

& [ImplementationShape] is one pure Rust module
  + [module] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_supplied_directory_topology_projection.rs
  + [export] is one public module declaration in cantor_ecosystem lib
  + [unit_tests] live beside the module
  + [static_test] is one independent source-surface test
  + [evidence_test] is one clone-portable manifest rehash test
  + [Cargo_delta] is zero
  + [lockfile_delta] is zero
  + [unsafe_delta] is zero
  + [platform_call_delta] is zero

& [DownstreamBoundary] remains separate
  + root-directory projection needs its own root binding and null-path contract
  + mixed-entry inventory reconciliation may consume output-only regular-file and directory projections only after its own source and SJS
  + physical production must preserve handle and query provenance under separate unsafe review and fixture authority
  + Git reconciliation needs a separate evidence vocabulary and producer contract
  + traversal, receipt, and admission require repeated whole-root evidence and freshness semantics not present here

& [SourceExit] is preservation before interpretation
  + preserve this file byte exactly with a separate manifest
  + do not overwrite it during explosion or canonical refinement
  + process it through the governing SJS protocol before implementation
  + bind the current supplied-entry-stability and M2A topology-form authorities
  + issue no implementation or execution authority merely from this source
